<title>SWEDEN: S-E-Banken 9 mo profit more than doubles.</title>
<headline>S-E-Banken 9 mo profit more than doubles.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish commercial bank S-E-Banken reports for the first nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     5,652 vs   5,670</p>
<p> Operating profit			  4,421 vs   2,060</p>
<p> Credit losses			     1,231 vs   3,610</p>
<p> EPS (SKR)				    6.33 vs    3.16</p>
<p> Interest receivable		    22,097 vs  22,885</p>
<p> Leasing income			    1,328 vs   1,264</p>
<p> Interest payable			 16,894 vs  18,258</p>
<p> Dividends received			  119 vs	89</p>
<p> Commission receivable		   4,074 vs   3,367</p>
<p> Commission payable			  642 vs     271</p>
<p> Net of fin trans	    CREDIT    2,590 vs   2,554   CREDIT</p>
<p> Other op income			     452 vs     988</p>
<p> Total income			     13,124 vs  12,618</p>
<p> Staff costs				 3,930 vs   3,499</p>
<p> Other admin costs			 1,653 vs   1,692</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,388 vs   1,278</p>
<p> Other op costs				501 vs     479</p>
<p> Total costs				 7,472 vs   6,948</p>
<p> Pension provisions			  124 vs     112</p>
<p> Tax					   1,209 vs     508</p>
<p> Net profit				  3,336 vs   1,664</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Swedish commercial bank is Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken. Analysts polled by Reuters expected an operating profit of 4.17 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
